WEBVTT

NOTE storefront weekly, 2026-09-02. Four speakers, twenty-eight minutes; the
NOTE cues below are the part the flywheel's meeting adapter reads. Storefront
NOTE is the shop — catalogue, cart, checkout — and payments is the service
NOTE that talks to the card processor.

1
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:21.500
<v Dana>Declines at checkout are up since Monday. It is not a handful, it
is most of a percent of every attempt, and it started on its own.

2
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:39.100
<v Priya>It is amex, mostly. I pulled a day of attempts and the amex share
of the declines is four times what it is of the traffic.

3
00:02:39.100 --> 00:03:02.400
<v Chuck>What does the retry do? Because I think it tries once, gets the
same answer back inside a second, and gives up. That is not a retry, that
is a second attempt at the same moment.

4
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:19.900
<v Priya>We do not log the processor's decline code. We log that it
declined. So I cannot tell you whether these are do-not-honour or
insufficient funds or something the retry would actually fix.

5
00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:37.200
<v Sam>Cart abandonment is up twelve per cent week on week. I do not know
that it is the same thing but the shape is the same and it started the
same day.

6
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:55.000
<v Chuck>We never wrote the retry policy down anywhere. It is whatever the
payments service does, and what it does is whatever someone typed in
eighteen months ago.

7
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:31.600
<v Sam>Separately — the catalogue images are slow on mobile. Two seconds
before anything paints on a mid-range phone. That is its own problem and I
keep forgetting to raise it.

8
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:52.300
<v Priya>Can we get a staging card processor? I cannot reproduce any of
this without putting real cards through production, which I would rather
not do.

9
00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:58.700
<v Dana>Coming back to it — the declines are up and we still do not know
why. I want that to be the thing we work on.
